    docs: render the operator's home as ~ in the generated conformance matrix -- the smoke leg now quotes the binary path it resolved, so the public artifact would otherwise publish a host layout. Addresses CF-225.
    
    The fix in 2f07051 made leg_smoke quote the path it resolved ("binary /home/<user>/.local/harness/npm/bin/claude ..."). Those values flow verbatim into docs/HARNESS-CONFORMANCE.md, which is generated and committed: a public repo would then carry the operator's home directory, the class CF-050 filed (16 rows already embed absolute /home paths).
    
    write_doc now pipes the generated body through sed 's|$HOME|~|g', and the run emits a battery:doc-home-path row that turns FAIL when the artifact still contains $HOME -- remove the sed and the row goes red, so the property is falsifiable rather than asserted.
    
    Measured on this host: regenerated docs/HARNESS-CONFORMANCE.md has 0 occurrences of /home/<user> (116 lines); the claude-code smoke cell reads
      SKIP -- ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or ~/.claude/.credentials.json
    and battery:doc-home-path prints PASS. tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS.
    
